Bstructure. It maintains a balanced,[39Gsorted[46Gtree[51Gof[54Gfixed-size[65Gpages,[72Gtypically[82Gwith[87Gvery[92Ghigh[97Gfanout[104Gso[107Gthe[111Gtree[116Gstays[2C[1Bshallow[11G(three[18Gor[21Gfour[26Glevels[33Gcovers[40Genormous[49Gdatasets).[60GThe[64Gkeys[69Glive[74Gin[77Gsorted[84Gorder[90Gacross[97Gleaf[102Gpages,[109Ginterior[2C[1Bpages hold separator keys and child pointers, and a mutation is p[69Grformed[77Gby finding [89Gh[91G page[97Gthat owns the key and[2C[1Bwriting the new value [3minto that page[23m, in plac[49G.[51GAn[54GLSM-tree (log-structured merge tre[89G) inverts this[104Gphilosophy:[116Gi[118G[K[2C[1Bnever mutates data where it lives. Writes accumul[53Gt[55G in an in-memory, sorted structure[90G(the memt[100Gble, often a skip[2C[1Blist or balanced [21Gree), backed by a[39Gwr[42Gte-ahead log[55Gfor durab[65Glity. When the[80Gmemtable fills, i[98G is[102Gflu[106Ghed as an[K[2C[1Bimmutable, sorted r[23Gn[25Gon disk (an SSTable). Over time you accumula[70Ge many such runs organiz[95Gd in[100Go levels, and a[116G[K[2C[1Bbackgro[11Gnd process[22G(compac[30Gion) merges and rewrites them to discard supe[76Gs[79Ged versions and[95Gk[97Gep read[105Gcosts[111Gbounded.[2C[1BSo [7Ghe essential[20Gcontrast is [3mmutate-in-place, read-optimized structure[23m versus [3mappend-mostly, write-optimized structure[2C[1Bthat pays down its debt later[23m.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mWrite amplification and the write path.[22m This is the LSM-tree's original reason for existing. A B-tree write, in the[K[2C[1Bworst realistic case, dirties a[35Gwhole[41Gpage[46Gto[49Gchange[56Ga[58Gfew[62Gbytes,[69Gand[73Gthat[78Gpage[83Gmust[88Geventually[99Gbe[102Gflushed[110Gto[113Gdisk[118G—[2C[1Bso[6Ga[8Gsmall[14Glogical[22Gwrite[28Gbecomes[36Ga[38Gfull-page[48Gphysical[57Gwrite[63G(and[68Gif[71Gyou[75Galso[80Gjournal[88Gvia[92Ga[